<LegalLayout title="Distance Sales Agreement" updated="August 2026">

<p>This Distance Sales Agreement is established between you ("the Buyer") and <strong>Cappadocia Kaphera Travel Agency</strong> (TÜRSAB No: 18577, "the Seller"), in accordance with the Turkish Law on Consumer Protection No. 6502 and the Distance Contracts Regulation, for tours, transfers and activities purchased through our website cappadociago.com using our online payment channel.</p>

<h2>1. Parties</h2>
<p><strong>Seller:</strong> Cappadocia Kaphera Travel Agency, Cappadocia, Nevşehir, Türkiye — TÜRSAB No: 18577 — <a href="mailto:info@kapheratravel.com">info@kapheratravel.com</a> — <a href="https://wa.me/905401015050">+90 540 101 50 50</a></p>
<p><strong>Buyer:</strong> The individual completing an online purchase on our website, whose details are recorded at the time of booking.</p>

<h2>2. Subject of the Agreement</h2>
<p>This Agreement covers the sale and delivery terms of the tour, activity, or transfer service selected and purchased by the Buyer through our website, including the service description, price, and payment method displayed at the time of purchase.</p>

<h2>3. General Terms</h2>
<ul>
  <li>By completing payment on our website, the Buyer confirms that the payment method used has been authorized by them.</li>
  <li>After purchase, the reservation is subject to confirmation by CappadociaGo. We reserve the right to confirm or decline a reservation based on availability.</li>
  <li>If a reservation cannot be confirmed, any payment made will be refunded to the original payment method within 5–10 business days, depending on the card issuer's processing time.</li>
  <li>The Buyer will be contacted by phone, WhatsApp or email the day before the scheduled tour or flight with final pickup time details.</li>
  <li>Pickup times are estimated in good faith based on travel distances; minor delays due to traffic conditions beyond our reasonable control do not constitute a breach of this Agreement.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Price &amp; Currency</h2>
<p>Prices are displayed in the currency selected by the Buyer at checkout. Where currency conversion is used, we apply the daily exchange rate published by the Central Bank of the Republic of Türkiye (TCMB). The final amount charged is confirmed to the Buyer before payment is completed.</p>

<h2>5. Right of Withdrawal</h2>
<p>In accordance with Turkish consumer protection legislation regarding services related to accommodation, transport, and leisure activities to be performed on a specific date, the right of withdrawal generally applicable to distance sales of goods does not apply once a specific tour date has been confirmed. Cancellation terms for tours and flights are governed separately by our <a href="/legal/cancellation-refund">Cancellation &amp; Refund Policy</a>.</p>

<h2>6. Force Majeure</h2>
<p>Neither party shall be held responsible for failure to perform obligations under this Agreement due to events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather preventing balloon flights, natural disasters, epidemics, government restrictions, or civil aviation authority decisions.</p>

<h2>7. Dispute Resolution</h2>
<p>Any disputes arising from this Agreement shall be resolved through the Consumer Arbitration Committees or Consumer Courts of Nevşehir, Türkiye, up to the monetary thresholds set annually by the Ministry of Trade, in accordance with Law No. 6502.</p>

<h2>8. Acceptance</h2>
<p>By completing an online purchase, the Buyer confirms they have read, understood, and accepted this Distance Sales Agreement in its entirety.</p>

